<title>CHILE: Chilgener mulls Colombia power stake sale.</title>
<headline>Chilgener mulls Colombia power stake sale.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean electricity firm Chilgener is studying selling a minority stake in its recently acquired Chivor power plant in Colombia, said finance and administration director Laurence Golborne.</p>
<p>&quot;It doesn't make any sense to hold onto 100 percent of the investment, but we are always keep 51 percent,&quot; Golborne told Reuters in an interview.</p>
<p>Chilgener, Chile's second largest power generator, bought the whole plant from the Colombian government for $643 million in December.</p>
</text>
